title: The reviewer found two bugs in the cycle, both fixed, and smaller things.
pid: 5b2c6543-4ade-4b47-95fc-88a463acecfa
body: |2-
  A fresh subagent reviewed the five cycle commits against Jeff's words.
  - High: "next" could skip an author for good. The set was estimated
    from what the buffer draws now, and a switch could hide the very
    node that put a later author in it. Fixed by judging each candidate
    by drawing the view from it, with candidates from both the root
    authors' drawing and the buffer's; its probe is now a test.
  - Medium: an author who changed nothing could join, beneath a node
    shown raw. Fixed by the same change.
  - Low, fixed: stale comments and a message, an end-of-file blank
    line, qualified paths in function bodies, a repeated literal,
    'owner of owner of X' in skg-for-ai, a multi-root naming test, a
    glossary entry for "perspective", and the docs on editing from
    another author's perspective.
  - Low, not done: an Emacs test of the retry after a privacy challenge
    (Neovim has one); a test of "owner of X" for a non-first skgrepo of
    a manifest-chained owner.
  It saw nothing to simplify in the clients.
